 ## How it works
-DropGaussian modifies the standard 3DGS training loop by introducing a stochastic dropout mechanism applied to the Gaussian primitives. The method addresses the issue where Gaussians far from the camera or occluded in sparse views receive insufficient gradient feedback, leading to overfitting [S1]. By randomly removing closer Gaussians, the visibility of distant Gaussians is improved, allowing them to receive larger gradients and contribute more effectively to the optimization [S1].
